   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "ANIME / CARTOON -> REAL PHONE PHOTO\n\n1. Load your anime or cartoon picture in '1. Anime / cartoon picture'.\n2. Press Run.\n\nThe prompt and negative prompt are ready. They ask for an ordinary smartphone photo and keep the same pose, outfit and every detail. Refer to the picture as <image1> if you edit them.\n\nSettings (tested): speed LoRA at 0.5, 12 steps, CFG 1.6, euler. CFG above 1 makes the negative prompt work against the drawn look. The speed LoRA at full strength with CFG 1 stays anime-looking. About 3 min per picture (the old 40-step version took 16).\n\nTips\n- Start ComfyUI with  comfyui h3  (the --fast-disk mode): the text encoder then runs on the GPU in ~30 s instead of ~5 min on the CPU.\n- Any picture size works: the size nodes shrink it to the megapixels you set. 1.0 is fast; 1.5 is sharper but slower.\n- Seed is random each Run. Press Run again for a different take.\n- Clear, front-lit photos where the face is big enough give the best results."
   ],
   "title": "How to use",
   "color": "#b06634",
   "bgcolor": "#353535",
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "ANIME / CARTOON -> REAL PHONE PHOTO\n\n1. Load your anime or cartoon picture in '1. Anime / cartoon picture'.\n2. Press Run.\n\nThe prompt and negative prompt are ready. They ask for an ordinary smartphone photo and keep the same pose, outfit and every detail. Refer to the picture as <image1> if you edit them.\n\nSettings (tested): speed LoRA at 0.5, 12 steps, CFG 1.6, euler. CFG above 1 makes the negative prompt work against the drawn look. The speed LoRA at full strength with CFG 1 stays anime-looking. About 3 min per picture (the old 40-step version took 16).\n\nTips\n- Start ComfyUI with  comfyui h3  (the --fast-disk mode): the text encoder then runs on the GPU in ~30 s instead of ~5 min on the CPU.\n- Any picture size works: the size nodes shrink it to the megapixels you set. 1.0 is fast; 1.5 is sharper but slower.\n- Seed is random each Run. Press Run again for a different take.\n- Clear, front-lit photos where the face is big enough give the best results."
   }
  },
